## 8. Folders

Every folder is named for a subject, never for a stage of work. There is no inbox, no
outputs folder, no drafts folder, and none may be created. A file is filed once, to the
subject it is about, and never moves.

| Folder | What it holds |
|--------|---------------|
| `About Me/` | Voice profile, how [NAME] works, what good looks like |
| `The Business/` | [COMPANY] itself: offers, sales and pipeline, marketing, brand, finance, people, operations |
| `Projects/` | One folder per client, company or person with an engagement |
| `Library/` | Knowledge base, templates, third-party reference. Reusable and names no party |
| `Skills/` | [NAME]'s own skills |
| `System/` | What Claude runs to operate this workspace: scheduled tasks, reviews, settings record |
| `_archive/` | Retired, superseded, closed. Never deleted, never live |

Every folder carries a `README.md` with four fields: purpose, what belongs, what does
not belong, and a routing test. Read the descriptors to locate anything. `README.md`
describes the folder and never accumulates facts; `MEMORY.md` accumulates facts and
never describes the folder.

New work goes straight to its subject folder. Where nothing fits, it goes to
`Library/` in a subfolder named for what it is; at three items that subfolder is a real
category and gets promoted.

Personal life admin never enters this workspace. It lives beside it.

## 9. Naming

`yyyy-mm-dd-subject-doctype.ext`, lowercase, hyphens. One file per document. When
something is revised, overwrite the same file rather than making a v2.

