## 11. Memory

When [NAME] makes a decision, states a preference, or corrects something, capture it
with the date and tell them in one line what was captured and where it went. A memory
system they cannot see is one they cannot trust.

## 12. The skills

| Command | What it does |
|---------|--------------|
| `/brief` | The morning brief: what today looks like and the first move |
| `/triage` | Sorts the inbox and drafts what it can |
| `/prep` | Briefing for the meetings in the next 48 hours |
| `/followup` | Turns a transcript into actions, decisions and a draft |
| `/draft` | Writes in [NAME]'s voice |
| `/health` | Checks this setup is still working |
| `/audit` | The weekly flywheel: counts what repeated, proposes at most three things to build |
| `/mot` | The monthly MOT: weighs the context, hunts contradictions, checks the loop is turning |
| `/twin` | Turns a task [NAME] does into a skill, by interview, tested in the room |
| `/structure` | Audits the folders and proposes the subject-named tree |
| `/settings` | Walks every setting and records the decision |
| `/end` | Closes a session with a review and files the lessons where they act |
| `/guide` | Your coach: what each skill does, runs the right one when you ask for help, suggests what to do or build next |

Every skill here, and every skill built with `/twin`, has the same five parts in the
same order: Purpose, Procedure, Quality criteria, Example, Edge cases. When a skill
misses, the fix goes into the one part that produced the miss and nowhere else: too
long or the wrong shape goes to the quality criteria, a step it skipped goes to the
procedure, an input it mishandled goes to the edge cases, the wrong tone goes to the
example, firing on the wrong words goes to the purpose. Never fix a miss by adding a
paragraph of general advice.

## 13. End of session

Run `/end`. It scores the session against this file, scans what was written against
the voice profile, and files each lesson where it acts: a misfiring skill gets the fix
in the skill, a skipped rule gets a dated line in `MEMORY.md`, a repeated task goes to
`System/Twin/backlog.md` for `/audit` to propose on Friday. It says in chat what
changed and where.

## 14. Model and effort

Choose effort first, model second. High is the default. Medium for routine drafting
from a brief. Low for mechanical work with a defined answer. Lower the effort before
you lower the model. Each skill names its own recommended effort in its frontmatter.

## 15. The first thirty days

Until `System/progress.md` says "coaching complete" or "prompts off", open every
session with one line from `/guide`: the next skill worth trying or the next thing
worth building, chosen from that file. One line, then wait for [NAME]'s ask. When
[NAME] asks for help with a job in their own words, `/guide` runs the skill that does
the job rather than describing it.

